{"id":8822,"date":"2025-10-12T14:22:35","date_gmt":"2025-10-12T14:22:35","guid":{"rendered":"https:\/\/www.usamasaleh.com\/?post_type=news&#038;p=8822"},"modified":"2025-11-30T14:29:24","modified_gmt":"2025-11-30T14:29:24","slug":"%f0%9f%93%b0-dr-usama-saleh-appointed-as-associate-clinical-professor-at-the-university-of-sharjah","status":"publish","type":"news","link":"https:\/\/usamasaleh.com\/news\/%f0%9f%93%b0-dr-usama-saleh-appointed-as-associate-clinical-professor-at-the-university-of-sharjah\/","title":{"rendered":"\ud83d\udcf0 Dr. Usama Saleh Appointed as Associate Clinical Professor at the University of Sharjah"},"content":{"rendered":"\n<p><strong>Sharjah, UAE \u2014<\/strong> Dr. Usama Saleh, Consultant Orthopedic Surgeon and one of the region\u2019s leading specialists in <strong>orthopedic and trauma surgery<\/strong>, has officially been appointed as <strong>Associate Clinical Professor at the University of Sharjah<\/strong>.<br><br>This prestigious recognition marks a new chapter in his distinguished career, celebrating his dual contribution to <strong>advanced orthopedic medicine<\/strong> and <strong>medical education<\/strong> in the United Arab Emirates.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p>For more than two decades, <strong>Dr. Usama Saleh<\/strong> has been at the forefront of <strong>orthopedic surgery, sports injury management, and joint reconstruction<\/strong>, earning a reputation for precision, empathy, and innovation in patient care.<br>His promotion to Associate Clinical Professor highlights his continuous dedication to knowledge sharing, clinical excellence, and the mentorship of the next generation of surgeons.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<blockquote class=\"wp-block-quote is-layout-flow wp-block-quote-is-layout-flow\">\n<p>\u201cHealing goes beyond the operating room,\u201d says Dr. Saleh. \u201cIt lives in every student who learns, every colleague who shares, and every patient who recovers. Teaching is simply another form of healing.\u201d<\/p>\n<\/blockquote>\n\n\n\n<p>At the <strong>University of Sharjah College of Medicine<\/strong>, Dr. Usama Saleh will lead advanced clinical sessions focused on <strong>orthopedic procedures<\/strong>, <strong>minimally invasive surgical techniques<\/strong>, and <strong>evidence-based rehabilitation approaches<\/strong>.<br>His vision is to bridge the gap between practice and academia\u2014ensuring that every future doctor learns the art of combining surgical mastery with compassion and ethical responsibility.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p>Dr. Saleh\u2019s medical journey began with a deep passion for restoring mobility and improving quality of life for his patients.<br>Over the years, he has performed hundreds of successful <strong>arthroscopic surgeries, joint replacements, and complex fracture treatments<\/strong>, always embracing the latest medical technologies and international standards of care.<br>His teaching philosophy reflects the same precision he brings to surgery: focused, detailed, and outcome-driven.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p>The appointment further strengthens <strong>the University of Sharjah\u2019s orthopedic training program<\/strong>, positioning it among the most respected academic centers for clinical education in the GCC region.<br>Students and residents under Dr. Saleh\u2019s mentorship will benefit from his hands-on experience in both <strong>clinical practice<\/strong> and <strong>academic research<\/strong>.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p>Beyond his clinical and academic responsibilities, Dr. Usama Saleh continues to advocate for <strong>patient education, preventive orthopedics, and the importance of early diagnosis<\/strong>.<br>He remains active in regional medical conferences, publishes research on advanced orthopedic solutions, and contributes to professional workshops focused on <strong>sports injuries<\/strong>, <strong>joint preservation<\/strong>, and <strong>rehabilitation innovations<\/strong>.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p>This milestone reinforces Dr. Usama Saleh\u2019s standing as a respected <strong>orthopedic consultant in Sharjah and Dubai<\/strong>, trusted by patients and colleagues alike for his expertise, mentorship, and leadership within the healthcare community.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<hr class=\"wp-block-separator has-alpha-channel-opacity\"\/>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>About Dr. Usama Saleh<\/strong><\/h3>\n\n\n\n<p><strong>Dr. Usama Saleh<\/strong> is an Orthopedic Consultant and Associate Clinical Professor at the University of Sharjah.<br>He specializes in <strong>arthroscopy, trauma surgery, sports medicine, and joint reconstruction<\/strong>.<br>Driven by a philosophy of healing through knowledge, Dr. Saleh continues to balance his clinical practice with teaching and research, inspiring future generations of medical professionals across the UAE and beyond.<\/p>\n","protected":false},"excerpt":{"rendered":"<p>Sharjah, UAE \u2014 Dr. Usama Saleh, Consultant Orthopedic Surgeon and one of the region\u2019s leading specialists in orthopedic and trauma surgery, has officially been appointed as Associate Clinical Professor at the University of Sharjah. This prestigious recognition marks a new chapter in his distinguished career, celebrating his dual contribution to advanced orthopedic medicine and medical education in the United Arab Emirates. For more than two decades, Dr. Usama Saleh has been at the forefront of orthopedic surgery, sports injury management, and joint reconstruction, earning a reputation for precision, empathy, and innovation in patient care.His promotion to Associate Clinical Professor highlights his continuous dedication to knowledge sharing, clinical excellence, and the mentorship of the next generation of surgeons. \u201cHealing goes beyond the operating room,\u201d says Dr. Saleh. \u201cIt lives in every student who learns, every colleague who shares, and every patient who recovers. Teaching is simply another form of healing.\u201d At the University of Sharjah College of Medicine, Dr. Usama Saleh will lead advanced clinical sessions focused on orthopedic procedures, minimally invasive surgical techniques, and evidence-based rehabilitation approaches.His vision is to bridge the gap between practice and academia\u2014ensuring that every future doctor learns the art of combining surgical mastery with compassion and ethical responsibility. Dr. Saleh\u2019s medical journey began with a deep passion for restoring mobility and improving quality of life for his patients.Over the years, he has performed hundreds of successful arthroscopic surgeries, joint replacements, and complex fracture treatments, always embracing the latest medical technologies and international standards of care.His teaching philosophy reflects the same precision he brings to surgery: focused, detailed, and outcome-driven. The appointment further strengthens the University of Sharjah\u2019s orthopedic training program, positioning it among the most respected academic centers for clinical education in the GCC region.Students and residents under Dr. Saleh\u2019s mentorship will benefit from his hands-on experience in both clinical practice and academic research. Beyond his clinical and academic responsibilities, Dr. Usama Saleh continues to advocate for patient education, preventive orthopedics, and the importance of early diagnosis.He remains active in regional medical conferences, publishes research on advanced orthopedic solutions, and contributes to professional workshops focused on sports injuries, joint preservation, and rehabilitation innovations. This milestone reinforces Dr. Usama Saleh\u2019s standing as a respected orthopedic consultant in Sharjah and Dubai, trusted by patients and colleagues alike for his expertise, mentorship, and leadership within the healthcare community. About Dr. Usama Saleh Dr. Usama Saleh is an Orthopedic Consultant and Associate Clinical Professor at the University of Sharjah.He specializes in arthroscopy, trauma surgery, sports medicine, and joint reconstruction.Driven by a philosophy of healing through knowledge, Dr. Saleh continues to balance his clinical practice with teaching and research, inspiring future generations of medical professionals across the UAE and beyond.<\/p>\n","protected":false},"featured_media":8777,"comment_status":"open","ping_status":"closed","template":"","class_list":["post-8822","news","type-news","status-publish","has-post-thumbnail","hentry"],"acf":[],"_links":{"self":[{"href":"https:\/\/usamasaleh.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/news\/8822","targetHints":{"allow":["GET"]}}],"collection":[{"href":"https:\/\/usamasaleh.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/news"}],"about":[{"href":"https:\/\/usamasaleh.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/types\/news"}],"replies":[{"embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/usamasaleh.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/comments?post=8822"}],"version-history":[{"count":1,"href":"https:\/\/usamasaleh.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/news\/8822\/revisions"}],"predecessor-version":[{"id":8823,"href":"https:\/\/usamasaleh.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/news\/8822\/revisions\/8823"}],"wp:featuredmedia":[{"embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/usamasaleh.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/media\/8777"}],"wp:attachment":[{"href":"https:\/\/usamasaleh.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/media?parent=8822"}],"curies":[{"name":"wp","href":"https:\/\/api.w.org\/{rel}","templated":true}]}}